{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Delivered a self-checking constrained-random testbench (tb/tb_crc8_block.v, top tb_crc8_block) for crc8_block. Its reference model is written from the interface specification. Platform simulation and independent review are still outstanding.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "testbench", "title": "Constrained-random self-checking testbench for crc8_block", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-91ad500fdf]. The testbench drives crc8_block through its ports only. The reference model is written from [artifact:prj-dbb4754f2d.interface-spec.a1] and does not reuse the per-bit loop structure of [artifact:prj-dbb4754f2d.design-under-test.a1]: it XORs the byte into the register, then makes 8 polynomial-0x07 shift steps. Checks run every cycle at two points. One sits just after the input change at the falling edge, and catches a crc that depends on inputs or an asynchronous reset. The other sits just after the rising edge and covers CRC-RESET, CRC-INIT, CRC-POLY, CRC-HOLD and CRC-FINAL. A directed phase uses literal expected values worked by hand from the spec. These cover CRC-EMPTY 0x00, single bytes 0xFF->0xFF, 0x00->0x0C, 0x01->0x0B and 0x80->0x85 (CRC-ORDER), two bytes 00 00->0x28, the priority of reset and init over valid, and the receiver residue 0x0C after the check value is appended. A random phase of 20000 cycles follows, with a printed, replayable seed and percentage knobs. It is biased toward 0x00/0xFF/one-hot bytes, reset or init on the same edge as valid, and resets in mid-frame. It also checks the literal 0x0C residue when random frames append their check value. Ten functional-coverage goals are each counted as a check, and a goal that is not reached fails the run. The testbench prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line, then calls $finish."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/tb_crc8_block.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "tb_crc8_block: constrained-random self-checking testbench for crc8_block", "summary": "Verilog-2001 testbench for Icarus or Verilator --binary. It instantiates crc8_block from [artifact:prj-dbb4754f2d.design-under-test.a1], and its reference model and literal expected values come from [artifact:prj-dbb4754f2d.interface-spec.a1]. It serves [requirement:req-91ad500fdf] with a directed phase, then a seeded random phase with coverage goals. Every compare adds to the pass or fail count. It prints one verdict line, NIRMAAN-SIM <nonce> <n> passed, <m> failed.", "entry": "tb_crc8_block"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The testbench has not been simulated by me. The 'testbench passes on the approved RTL' requirement still has to be met by the platform's simulator.run.", "The literal expected values (0x00, 0xFF, 0x0C, 0x0B, 0x85, 0x28, and residue 0x0C) were worked by hand from the specification and have not been tool-checked. A hand-arithmetic error would show up as a failure on the clean RTL.", "My four sections do not name the plusarg that carries the run nonce. The testbench tries nonce=, NONCE=, nirmaan_nonce=, NIRMAAN_NONCE= and NIRMAAN_SIM_NONCE=. If none is present, it reports a failed check and prints MISSING as the nonce.", "The coverage minimums (for example at least 20 resets on the same edge as valid) are set well below the expected counts for 20000 cycles at the default seed. Whether each goal is reached is not confirmed until the run.", "A single fixed default seed is used, overridable with +seed=<n>. Multi-seed regression is not part of this deliverable."], "escalation": null, "notes": "The main source of uncertainty is the plusarg name for the nonce, which my inputs do not give. If the platform uses another name, the verdict carries MISSING and the run fails; adding one $value$plusargs line fixes it. I chose this over escalating because the rest of the deliverable does not depend on it. Design choices: inputs are driven at the falling edge and sampled 1 ns after each edge, so the testbench does not race the design. The crc is compared both before and after each rising edge, so a mutant with asynchronous reset or a combinational crc fails. The literal known-answer vectors anchor the model independently, so the model cannot pass simply by agreeing with the RTL. Independent review (P6) is still required and must be done by another seat."}
=== FILE: tb/tb_crc8_block.v ===
// Self-checking constrained-random testbench for crc8_block.
// Reference model and expected values written from interface_spec.md
// (req CRC-RESET, CRC-INIT, CRC-POLY, CRC-ORDER, CRC-HOLD, CRC-FINAL, CRC-EMPTY),
// not from the RTL. Prints exactly one verdict line, then calls $finish.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module tb_crc8_block;

    // ---------------- knobs ----------------
    localparam integer N_RANDOM  = 20000; // random-phase cycles
    localparam integer P_RST     = 2;     // % cycles with rst_n low
    localparam integer P_INIT    = 8;     // % non-reset cycles with init high
    localparam integer P_VALID   = 70;    // % plain cycles with valid high
    localparam integer P_APPEND  = 5;     // % plain cycles that append the check value
    localparam integer MAX_FAIL_PRINT = 20;

    // ---------------- DUT ----------------
    reg        clk;
    reg        rst_n;
    reg        init;
    reg        valid;
    reg  [7:0] data;
    wire [7:0] crc;

    crc8_block dut (
        .clk   (clk),
        .rst_n (rst_n),
        .init  (init),
        .valid (valid),
        .data  (data),
        .crc   (crc)
    );

    initial clk = 1'b0;
    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    // ---------------- bookkeeping ----------------
    integer pass_count;
    integer fail_count;
    integer seed;
    reg [31:0] rnd;

    reg [7:0] model;        // running value per spec section 2
    reg       model_known;  // becomes 1 at the first reset or reload edge

    // corner / coverage counters
    integer bytes_taken, holds;
    integer rst_edges, rst_with_valid, rst_with_init, rst_midframe;
    integer init_edges, init_with_valid, init_midframe;
    integer data00, dataFF, residue_checks;
    integer bytes_since_reload;

    // nonce
    reg [8*256-1:0] nonce;
    reg             nonce_found;
    integer         ci;
    reg [7:0]       ch;

    // ---------------- reference model (from the spec) ----------------
    // Spec 2.2: per bit, MSB first, XOR the bit into the top bit, shift left,
    // XOR 0x07 if the bit shifted out was 1. For an 8-bit CRC this equals
    // XORing the whole byte into the running value, then 8 shift steps.
    function [7:0] ref_take_byte;
        input [7:0] run;
        input [7:0] b;
        integer k;
        reg [7:0] v;
        begin
            v = run ^ b;
            for (k = 0; k < 8; k = k + 1) begin
                if (v[7])
                    v = {v[6:0], 1'b0} ^ 8'h07;
                else
                    v = {v[6:0], 1'b0};
            end
            ref_take_byte = v;
        end
    endfunction

    // ---------------- checking ----------------
    task check;
        input [8*48-1:0] tag;
        input [7:0]      exp;
        begin
            if (crc !== exp) begin
                fail_count = fail_count + 1;
                if (fail_count <= MAX_FAIL_PRINT)
                    $display("CHECK FAIL t=%0t [%0s] crc=%h expected=%h (rst_n=%b init=%b valid=%b data=%h)",
                             $time, tag, crc, exp, rst_n, init, valid, data);
            end else begin
                pass_count = pass_count + 1;
            end
        end
    endtask

    task cov_check;
        input [8*40-1:0] tag;
        input integer    count;
        input integer    minimum;
        begin
            if (count < minimum) begin
                fail_count = fail_count + 1;
                $display("COVERAGE FAIL [%0s] reached %0d, goal %0d", tag, count, minimum);
            end else begin
                pass_count = pass_count + 1;
                $display("coverage ok   [%0s] reached %0d, goal %0d", tag, count, minimum);
            end
        end
    endtask

    // One clock cycle: drive at the falling edge, check that crc still holds
    // the old value (no input dependence, synchronous reset), update the model
    // at the rising edge, then check after the edge.
    task cycle;
        input       r;
        input       i;
        input       v;
        input [7:0] d;
        begin
            @(negedge clk);
            rst_n = r; init = i; valid = v; data = d;
            #1;
            if (model_known) check("between edges: crc must not move", model ^ 8'hFF);
            @(posedge clk);
            if (!r) begin
                model = 8'hFF; model_known = 1'b1;
                rst_edges = rst_edges + 1;
                if (v) rst_with_valid = rst_with_valid + 1;
                if (i) rst_with_init  = rst_with_init + 1;
                if (bytes_since_reload > 0) rst_midframe = rst_midframe + 1;
                bytes_since_reload = 0;
            end else if (i) begin
                model = 8'hFF; model_known = 1'b1;
                init_edges = init_edges + 1;
                if (v) init_with_valid = init_with_valid + 1;
                if (bytes_since_reload > 0) init_midframe = init_midframe + 1;
                bytes_since_reload = 0;
            end else if (v) begin
                model = ref_take_byte(model, d);
                bytes_taken = bytes_taken + 1;
                bytes_since_reload = bytes_since_reload + 1;
                if (d == 8'h00) data00 = data00 + 1;
                if (d == 8'hFF) dataFF = dataFF + 1;
            end else begin
                holds = holds + 1;
            end
            #1;
            if (model_known) check("after edge: crc vs model", model ^ 8'hFF);
        end
    endtask

    // ---------------- random helpers ----------------
    task rand100;
        output integer x;
        begin
            rnd = $random(seed);
            x = rnd % 100;
        end
    endtask

    task pick_data;
        output [7:0] d;
        integer roll;
        begin
            rand100(roll);
            if (roll < 10)       d = 8'h00;
            else if (roll < 20)  d = 8'hFF;
            else if (roll < 30) begin
                rnd = $random(seed);
                d = 8'h01 << rnd[2:0];
            end else begin
                rnd = $random(seed);
                d = rnd[7:0];
            end
        end
    endtask

    // ---------------- watchdog ----------------
    reg done;
    initial begin
        done = 1'b0;
        #10000000;
        if (!done) begin
            $display("TIMEOUT: testbench did not complete");
            fail_count = fail_count + 1;
            print_verdict;
            $finish;
        end
    end

    task print_verdict;
        begin
            $write("NIRMAAN-SIM ");
            if (nonce_found) begin
                for (ci = 255; ci >= 0; ci = ci - 1) begin
                    ch = nonce[ci*8 +: 8];
                    if (ch != 8'h00) $write("%c", ch);
                end
            end else begin
                $write("MISSING");
            end
            $write(" %0d passed, %0d failed\n", pass_count, fail_count);
        end
    endtask

    // ---------------- main ----------------
    integer n, roll, x;
    reg     r_r, r_i, r_v, is_app;
    reg [7:0] r_d;

    initial begin
        pass_count = 0; fail_count = 0;
        model = 8'hFF; model_known = 1'b0;
        bytes_taken = 0; holds = 0;
        rst_edges = 0; rst_with_valid = 0; rst_with_init = 0; rst_midframe = 0;
        init_edges = 0; init_with_valid = 0; init_midframe = 0;
        data00 = 0; dataFF = 0; residue_checks = 0; bytes_since_reload = 0;
        rst_n = 1'b0; init = 1'b0; valid = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;

        nonce = 0;
        nonce_found = 1'b0;
        if ($value$plusargs("nonce=%s", nonce))                  nonce_found = 1'b1;
        else if ($value$plusargs("NONCE=%s", nonce))             nonce_found = 1'b1;
        else if ($value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))     nonce_found = 1'b1;
        else if ($value$plusargs("NIRMAAN_NONCE=%s", nonce))     nonce_found = 1'b1;
        else if ($value$plusargs("NIRMAAN_SIM_NONCE=%s", nonce)) nonce_found = 1'b1;

        seed = 32'h0C2C_0807;
        if ($value$plusargs("seed=%d", x)) seed = x;
        $display("tb_crc8_block: seed=%0d (replay with +seed=%0d)", seed, seed);

        // ---------- directed phase: literal values worked from the spec ----------
        cycle(1'b0, 1'b0, 1'b0, 8'h00);
        cycle(1'b0, 1'b0, 1'b0, 8'h00);
        check("CRC-RESET/CRC-EMPTY: 0x00 after reset", 8'h00);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b1, 8'hFF);
        check("one byte 0xFF gives 0xFF", 8'hFF);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b1, 1'b0, 8'h00);
        check("CRC-EMPTY: 0x00 after init", 8'h00);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b1, 8'h00);
        check("one byte 0x00 gives 0x0C", 8'h0C);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b1, 8'h00);
        check("bytes 00 00 give 0x28", 8'h28);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b0, 8'hA5);
        check("CRC-HOLD: valid low keeps 0x28", 8'h28);
        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b0, 8'h3C);
        check("CRC-HOLD: valid low keeps 0x28 (2)", 8'h28);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b1, 8'h28);
        check("residue 0x0C after appending crc", 8'h0C);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b1, 1'b1, 8'h5A);
        check("CRC-INIT: init wins over valid", 8'h00);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b1, 8'h01);
        check("CRC-ORDER: byte 0x01 gives 0x0B", 8'h0B);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b1, 1'b0, 8'h00);
        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b1, 8'h80);
        check("CRC-ORDER: byte 0x80 gives 0x85", 8'h85);

        cycle(1'b0, 1'b0, 1'b1, 8'h33);
        check("CRC-RESET: reset wins over valid", 8'h00);

        cycle(1'b0, 1'b1, 1'b1, 8'h33);
        check("CRC-RESET: reset with init and valid", 8'h00);

        cycle(1'b1, 1'b0, 1'b0, 8'h00);
        check("hold after reset stays 0x00", 8'h00);

        // ---------- constrained-random phase ----------
        for (n = 0; n < N_RANDOM; n = n + 1) begin
            r_r = 1'b1; r_i = 1'b0; r_v = 1'b0; r_d = 8'h00; is_app = 1'b0;
            rand100(roll);
            if (roll < P_RST) begin
                r_r = 1'b0;
                rand100(x); r_i = (x < 30);
                rand100(x); r_v = (x < 50);
                pick_data(r_d);
            end else begin
                rand100(roll);
                if (roll < P_INIT) begin
                    r_i = 1'b1;
                    rand100(x); r_v = (x < 60);
                    pick_data(r_d);
                end else begin
                    rand100(roll);
                    if (roll < P_APPEND && bytes_since_reload > 0) begin
                        r_v = 1'b1;
                        r_d = model ^ 8'hFF;   // sender appends the check value
                        is_app = 1'b1;
                    end else begin
                        rand100(x); r_v = (x < P_VALID);
                        pick_data(r_d);
                    end
                end
            end
            cycle(r_r, r_i, r_v, r_d);
            if (is_app) begin
                check("residue 0x0C after appended check value", 8'h0C);
                residue_checks = residue_checks + 1;
            end
        end

        // ---------- coverage goals (fail the run if not reached) ----------
        cov_check("bytes taken",                bytes_taken,     5000);
        cov_check("hold cycles",                holds,           1000);
        cov_check("init with valid same edge",  init_with_valid, 50);
        cov_check("init in mid-frame",          init_midframe,   50);
        cov_check("reset with valid same edge", rst_with_valid,  20);
        cov_check("reset with init same edge",  rst_with_init,   5);
        cov_check("reset in mid-frame",         rst_midframe,    20);
        cov_check("data byte 0x00",             data00,          100);
        cov_check("data byte 0xFF",             dataFF,          100);
        cov_check("residue checks",             residue_checks,  100);

        if (!nonce_found) begin
            $display("ERROR: no nonce plusarg found");
            fail_count = fail_count + 1;
        end

        $display("tb_crc8_block: seed=%0d cycles=%0d resets=%0d inits=%0d", seed, N_RANDOM, rst_edges, init_edges);
        done = 1'b1;
        print_verdict;
        $finish;
    end

endmodule
=== END FILE ===
